    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d840">

                <pb facs="0816" n="804" xml:id="pg804"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">867N.01/1898: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-08-10T16:00:00+02:00">August 10, 1943—4
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received August 10—11:30 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5235. In accordance with the Department’s 4767, August 7, 5 p.m., I informed Mr.
                    Eden of the decision not to issue the proposed joint statement regarding
                    Palestine. He and Colonel Stanley<anchor n="87" xml:id="d840-f1"/> were both
                    very disappointed.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d840-f1" n="87" xml:id="d840-f1-content">
                <p>Col. Oliver Stanley, British Colonial Secretary.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
